{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"No. Indigenous people are genetically diverse, both within individual communities and across populations worldwide. “Indigenous” describes peoples’ historical, cultural, and political relationships to their homelands; it is not a single genetic category.\n\nAll humans share the vast majority of their DNA, but that does not make Indigenous people—or members of any other broad group—genetically identical. Indigenous identity also cannot be determined by DNA alone."}}
